{
  "description": "Hand-labeled ground truth for NovaClaim AI's synthetic prior authorization test set. All documents are synthetic: names, member IDs, NPIs and authorization numbers are invented. null means the field is not present in the document, and the correct extraction is to return nothing.",
  "labeling_rules": [
    "approval_date is the payer's decision date, matching the parser prompt ('Decision date'). Denied documents use their Decision Date. It is null when no decision has been made (Pending, or 'Decision Date: N/A').",
    "The request date ('DATE OF REQUEST' / 'Date:') is never the approval_date. Extracting it there counts as a hallucination.",
    "authorization_number is null for denied and pending requests. 'Group Number' is not an authorization number.",
    "provider_npi is the individual provider's NPI. test_real_npi.txt also lists a Facility NPI as a deliberate distractor.",
    "Short-form documents combine payer and plan into one 'Insurance Plan' line. They are labeled as payer = carrier name and plan_name = the remainder (e.g. 'Cigna Open Access Plus' -> payor 'Cigna', plan 'Open Access Plus').",
    "Honorifics and credentials (Dr., MD) are not part of provider_name."
  ],
  "fields": [
    "patient_name", "date_of_birth", "member_id", "provider_name", "provider_npi",
    "facility_name", "diagnosis_code", "treatment_requested", "cpt_code", "payor",
    "plan_name", "approval_status", "approval_date", "authorization_number"
  ],
